  "notes": "Source table includes all retired members and beneficiaries (Service, Disability, and Survivors) as the document does not provide a separate table for Service Retirees only. The '50 & Under' bin is mapped to '50-54' via sum (assuming negligible counts below 50 for this plan). The 'Over 80' bin is split evenly across '80-84' and '85-89' via share_even. Target rows '90-94', '95-99', and '100 & over' have no source data. The 'Average Annual Benefits' column in the source is derived from Total/Count, so the target AverageBenefit is declared as a ratio of the Total Annual Benefits and Number of Members columns to ensure exact alignment with the split counts. The 'Number' column uses 'sum' with 'weights_table' 0 to correctly compute the weighted average for the 'AverageBenefit' column when bins are merged.",
